WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.501
Tomorrow's your day to die.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.584
What's your last meal?

00:00:03.751 --> 00:00:06.042
Filthy, dirty, buttery potatoes,

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:08.042
with a beautiful Sauvignon Blanc

00:00:08.042 --> 00:00:09.792
from the Marlborough region of New Zealand,

00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:12.042
and old school prawn cocktail.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.209
And you?

00:00:13.209 --> 00:00:16.167
A really beautiful cut in half avocado

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:19.042
with fresh vine ripe tomatoes and a little bit of mozzerella,

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:21.250
and a really good Spaghetti Bolognese. 

00:00:25.459 --> 00:00:27.209
How did Rebecca come into your life?

00:00:27.209 --> 00:00:30.292
I got the pilot sent through

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:33.584
in a kind of secret squirrel type way. 

00:00:33.584 --> 00:00:35.918
One of those, like weird, where you can’t...

00:00:35.918 --> 00:00:37.000
You can see this, but you can't see this. 

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.042
On one device, yeah. 

00:00:38.042 --> 00:00:39.542
You know it exists, but you don't.

00:00:39.542 --> 00:00:40.375
Mhm. 

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:44.292
And um, yeah, I wasn't told what it was for,

00:00:44.292 --> 00:00:46.751
who it was for, who'd created it. 

00:00:46.751 --> 00:00:47.501
Nothing.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:50.459
But that actually afforded me the luxury

00:00:50.459 --> 00:00:52.918
to just go, oh who is this woman 

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:54.334
at face value.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.000
That's the first time, I think ever

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.751
because it was so secret squirrel,

00:00:57.751 --> 00:00:58.667
do you have a, is there a different 

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.083
expression in America for that? 

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:01.542
Like secret badger or something?

00:01:01.542 --> 00:01:03.292
Um, it's just like top secret, right?

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:04.083
It’s almost like… 

00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:05.334
So not secret squirrel.

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.792
Well no but I love that, you know. 

00:01:08.459 --> 00:01:10.918
Um, so then I just learned, learned all the sides 

00:01:10.918 --> 00:01:13.542
and went into town to a casting,

00:01:13.542 --> 00:01:15.459
and I don't know about you,

00:01:15.459 --> 00:01:18.709
but I just, I, I go (gibberish)

00:01:18.709 --> 00:01:20.417
leave what you think is the best

00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:21.959
you can do on camera

00:01:21.959 --> 00:01:24.918
and I always come out and tear it up. 

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.209
Me too 'cause also you want to leave it 

00:01:26.209 --> 00:01:27.375
in the room when it's that top secret.

00:01:27.375 --> 00:01:28.292
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:28.292 --> 00:01:29.584
You’re like, don’t give me the responsibility!

00:01:29.584 --> 00:01:31.292
It can't be in my recycling, oh my god.

00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:32.250
Because if that gets out...

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.501
With my name on it!

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:34.042
Exactly. 

00:01:34.042 --> 00:01:35.125
I'd kind of forgotten about it. 

00:01:35.125 --> 00:01:36.751
and went back to being Mama,

00:01:36.751 --> 00:01:38.209
picking my girl up from school.

00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:40.626
And then the day it, they said no you’ve got it,

00:01:40.626 --> 00:01:42.792
I had to go and pick my daughter up from school,

00:01:42.792 --> 00:01:44.626
walk through the very, very normal playground

00:01:44.626 --> 00:01:47.334
and not go, oh my god my life just changed! 

00:01:47.626 --> 00:01:49.292
If your house went up in flames,

00:01:49.292 --> 00:01:50.334
what would be the things you would grab?

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:53.083
It would be my girl, over my shoulder 

00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:54.209
and I'm good to go. 

00:02:00.918 --> 00:02:02.959
You've known Jason for ages, haven't you?

00:02:02.959 --> 00:02:06.000
I knew him for a little while yeah, beforehand 

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.501
and I'd been working in Europe for about six months. 

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.375
Got back to LA,

00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:13.083
turned thirty which was epic, 

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:14.250
don't tell anyone. 

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.375
That is quite a long time ago for me. 

00:02:15.375 --> 00:02:16.375
Don't tell anyone.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.167
Twenty-eight forever.

00:02:18.709 --> 00:02:20.667
But I got a text from Jason

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.834
being like, "Yo yo, uh, Jason here."

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:24.459
"Got your number."

00:02:24.459 --> 00:02:26.751
"and, uh just want to chat to you about something."

00:02:26.751 --> 00:02:30.626
to which I thought, oh he thinks I’m someone else.

00:02:30.626 --> 00:02:32.042
Oh no.

00:02:32.042 --> 00:02:33.167
I love your faith in yourself. 

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:35.334
So, so yeah, well I’m working on that.

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:37.667
But so then he, I was like

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.834
“Hey, what can I do for you?”

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.000
and he said well I actually have this pilot

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.167
that I would love you to read if you have a moment

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.584
or if you would be interested.

00:02:45.584 --> 00:02:47.792
It’s something that I am reaching out to you personally

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:49.542
about because it means a lot to me. 

00:02:49.542 --> 00:02:51.417
And so, I was like, are you kidding me?

00:02:51.417 --> 00:02:53.375
Quietly thinking, what if it’s not meant for me,

00:02:53.375 --> 00:02:54.667
like this is a disaster.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:55.959
So I did read it 

00:02:55.959 --> 00:02:58.417
and I just thought it was such an unusual pilot.

00:02:58.417 --> 00:02:59.584
I hadn't read anything like it

00:02:59.584 --> 00:03:01.375
'cause it made you laugh and also made you

00:03:01.375 --> 00:03:03.542
feel really emotional from the get-go,

00:03:03.542 --> 00:03:04.459
You know?

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:06.083
And, so then I called him

00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:08.083
and when he said, "Hey Juno!"

00:03:08.083 --> 00:03:10.042
I was like aah.

00:03:10.042 --> 00:03:10.876
There has been no confusion. 

00:03:10.876 --> 00:03:12.000
It was for me!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.792
You and I come from two such

00:03:14.792 --> 00:03:16.459
totally different comfort zones 

00:03:16.459 --> 00:03:17.876
You are nervous doing comedy,

00:03:17.876 --> 00:03:20.209
which nobody would believe on camera,

00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:21.167
and I come from...

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:21.751
The world of theater.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.125
Big sell was he did talk to me

00:03:28.125 --> 00:03:30.250
about this relationship between the two of us.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.250
Which was one that first and foremost

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.209
he was really passionate about

00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:36.459
and really cared about these two women

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:38.000
helping each other in ways

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.542
they didn’t know were even possible.

00:03:40.542 --> 00:03:41.459
So you knew about 

00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:42.876
I didn’t know anything about this relationship.

00:03:42.876 --> 00:03:44.417
I knew there was going to be

00:03:44.417 --> 00:03:46.709
this relationship that blossomed.

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:48.292
And I didn’t know the specifics of it.

00:03:48.292 --> 00:03:49.584
Like when I read that script

00:03:49.584 --> 00:03:51.667
that where it immediately is about

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:52.918
about you naked on a yacht

00:03:52.918 --> 00:03:54.751
and that’s so specific and I push you,

00:03:54.751 --> 00:03:56.209
push you and push you to see it because

00:03:56.209 --> 00:03:57.709
I’m like come on, you were dying to show someone.

00:03:57.709 --> 00:03:58.626
Yeah.

00:03:58.626 --> 00:04:01.292
And that moment of you kind of being like oh,

00:04:01.292 --> 00:04:02.459
I actually should be proud of

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:04.334
my beauty as a woman.

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.042
and it’s special where it is

00:04:06.042 --> 00:04:07.542
on this couch right here, isn’t it?

00:04:07.542 --> 00:04:09.751
Like Rebecca in her formality.

00:04:09.751 --> 00:04:11.876
Even the shape of what that scene looked like.

00:04:11.876 --> 00:04:13.918
And it’s a real turning point.

00:04:13.918 --> 00:04:16.125
And I think it’s the first time in a while

00:04:16.125 --> 00:04:17.584
that Rebecca has heard a compliment

00:04:17.584 --> 00:04:19.250
from a female that she’s believed 

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.250
I felt in that moment.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.459
Because I’m not sure either of

00:04:21.459 --> 00:04:24.209
these women have experienced

00:04:24.209 --> 00:04:26.501
love and friendship like you say

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:27.542
from another female

00:04:27.542 --> 00:04:29.751
and very much of different generations.

00:04:29.751 --> 00:04:31.334
It feels like they are kind of soul mates,

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:32.501
but they didn’t know that until 

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.709
episodes start progressing and

00:04:34.709 --> 00:04:37.125
by the end of season one I truly believe that.

00:04:37.125 --> 00:04:38.501
And then there’s the twist that happens

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:39.709
at the end that I know we’ve talked about. 

00:04:39.709 --> 00:04:41.000
Being able to call each other out.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:41.834
Being accountable.

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:42.459
Yeah.

00:04:42.459 --> 00:04:43.959
But it’s scary isn’t it and I think like

00:04:43.959 --> 00:04:45.667
as two women sitting here talking

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:46.417
about these characters,

00:04:46.417 --> 00:04:49.709
we can relate to them on such deep levels.

00:04:49.709 --> 00:04:50.626
I know you can.

00:04:50.626 --> 00:04:53.834
Your, your insight into Rebecca as a woman

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.709
is something that I watch as

00:04:55.709 --> 00:04:57.501
we've done press together about it.

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:59.083
And learning about how much

00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:01.209
she meant to you in a

00:05:01.209 --> 00:05:03.542
deep, deep way that makes you have such

00:05:03.542 --> 00:05:05.250
understanding of her which is why

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.584
she is such an extraordinary character in this.

00:05:07.584 --> 00:05:09.876
When you first started playing Rebecca,

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.667
do you feel they made her more

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:14.167
in tune with Hannah?

00:05:14.709 --> 00:05:18.375
Yeah, I think I felt a shift around the...

00:05:18.375 --> 00:05:19.959
Oh my god, the scene at the gala

00:05:19.959 --> 00:05:21.250
outside with you and Jason.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:21.792
Yes.

00:05:21.792 --> 00:05:24.250
That was probably more personal than anything?

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.167
Yeah, yeah it was.

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:26.709
Yeah, because I think by then,

00:05:26.709 --> 00:05:27.375
Yeah.

00:05:27.375 --> 00:05:29.542
I think by then, Jason, I mean he was lit...

00:05:29.542 --> 00:05:30.667
you know what he’s like fiddling

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.042
around with scripts and writing up

00:05:32.042 --> 00:05:33.000
up against a wall with Brett.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:33.918
SNL world. 

00:05:33.918 --> 00:05:34.667
I mean, yeah.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:35.501
Can learn lines like that. 

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.876
Yeah, I balked at that.

00:05:36.876 --> 00:05:38.542
I was like oh my god you can’t

00:05:38.542 --> 00:05:41.042
give me something like 10 minutes

00:05:41.042 --> 00:05:42.542
before we’re gonna be on camera

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.792
and he still did because he knew

00:05:44.792 --> 00:05:46.501
that I was limiting myself.

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:48.918
 And I was just like this is getting ridiculous

00:05:48.918 --> 00:05:51.542
how close to my life this has been.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:54.334
Our girlfriends are the most important people.

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:55.083
Oh my god, yeah.

00:05:55.083 --> 00:05:57.250
They ground us, they save our lives,

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.042
and hopefully we do the same for them.

00:05:59.042 --> 00:06:00.083
Undoubtedly.

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:07.209
Just the grace and ease of which you are a mother,

00:06:07.209 --> 00:06:10.292
you are an extraordinary actress,

00:06:10.292 --> 00:06:13.250
and you are a woman in a way that I,

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:16.000
I’m excited to grow up and be a woman because of it

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.042
I think it’s a very inspirational package.

00:06:18.042 --> 00:06:19.125
No one could have played

00:06:19.125 --> 00:06:21.375
this character Rebecca better.

00:06:21.375 --> 00:06:22.042
You know that,

00:06:22.042 --> 00:06:23.918
you know that 'cause you understand it all.

00:06:23.918 --> 00:06:25.751
You know I am horrendous with compliments.

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.125
But I feel the same about you,

00:06:27.125 --> 00:06:29.334
and it’s, and I can’t believe my luck

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:30.792
that you were even back for season two.

00:06:30.792 --> 00:06:32.959
I thought she’s so big-time she’ll be like off.

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:33.751
Oh come on. 

00:06:33.751 --> 00:06:35.751
Suddenly go, I’ll suddenly hear

00:06:35.751 --> 00:06:36.834
Juno’s not coming back to this.

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:38.501
No no no, because she’s doing this giant

00:06:38.501 --> 00:06:39.334
thing somewhere in outer Mongolia.

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:40.876
She saved my mental health.

00:06:40.876 --> 00:06:43.042
I wouldn’t want to miss this for the world.

00:06:43.042 --> 00:06:45.167
This whole cast, this crew, like everybody,

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:46.792
this character is like.

00:06:46.792 --> 00:06:49.375
Sure, I love the darkness, you know I do.

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.417
But I also, when we sit here, I get stopped

00:06:51.417 --> 00:06:52.417
in a grocery store with someone going like 

00:06:52.417 --> 00:06:53.709
“Hey, did I go to school with you?"

00:06:53.709 --> 00:06:56.250
"Oh no, I’ve just seen your boobs in a movie."

00:06:56.626 --> 00:06:58.209
And you're like over Cheerios in the

00:06:58.209 --> 00:07:00.375
Trader Joe’s or something, it’s like um…

00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:01.542
I know, but I have told you before you

00:07:01.542 --> 00:07:02.834
 have to celebrate the fact that people

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:04.918
 say that because they are magnificent.

00:07:04.918 --> 00:07:05.459
Great.

00:07:05.459 --> 00:07:06.000
All of it is. 

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.334
I mean, touché. Touché.

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:10.459
But I think like the fact that we get to

00:07:10.459 --> 00:07:14.083
do it one more time, is like thank God.

00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:15.792
I was literally just about to say

00:07:15.792 --> 00:07:17.709
what does that make you feel

00:07:17.709 --> 00:07:19.792
about wrapping on season two?

00:07:19.792 --> 00:07:21.501
Proud, but also really nervous

00:07:21.501 --> 00:07:24.000
because you’re just like,

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.083
you just want to make people proud.

00:07:26.083 --> 00:07:28.209
Now that we know about the success of season one,

00:07:28.209 --> 00:07:30.501
you just hope that people also respond to it

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:33.959
in a way that they love our character journeys 

00:07:33.959 --> 00:07:35.501
and still connect with them in a way

00:07:35.501 --> 00:07:36.459
that they did with season one

00:07:36.459 --> 00:07:38.125
even if they bring different emotions

00:07:38.125 --> 00:07:39.292
 and new journeys and all that.

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:41.792
Yeah, I think season two is quite different

00:07:41.792 --> 00:07:42.417
So do I. 

00:07:42.417 --> 00:07:45.542
In terms of really getting into the dirt.

00:07:45.542 --> 00:07:47.334
Yeah, exactly the human side of it

00:07:47.334 --> 00:07:48.542
which we all bottle up.

00:07:48.542 --> 00:07:50.292
that we don’t necessarily talk about.

00:07:50.292 --> 00:07:52.042
I think they should have a jelly fight

00:07:52.042 --> 00:07:53.542
in season three and really go for it.

00:07:53.542 --> 00:07:55.209
Or a pillow fight,

00:07:55.209 --> 00:07:56.584
in a hotel room.

00:07:56.584 --> 00:07:57.709
Or a bath.

00:07:58.501 --> 00:07:59.501
I just keep pushing.

00:08:04.209 --> 00:08:06.501
Our extraordinary female writers

00:08:06.501 --> 00:08:08.876
do us such a great service.

00:08:08.876 --> 00:08:09.417
Yeah.

00:08:09.417 --> 00:08:11.834
You know, and one storyline in particular

00:08:11.834 --> 00:08:14.501
that I have this year, I even spoke to Jason about it

00:08:14.501 --> 00:08:16.792
and I was like who’s mainly responsible for this

00:08:16.792 --> 00:08:18.667
and he said well they are and they are.

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:21.417
And I was like I need to go give them a squeeze

00:08:21.417 --> 00:08:23.334
and go come on the girls!

00:08:23.334 --> 00:08:25.584
'cause it’s just blindsided me

00:08:25.584 --> 00:08:28.125
and I love that they have literally gone

00:08:28.125 --> 00:08:30.209
go on, do that that gets you

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:31.250
out of your comfort zone.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:32.459
Yeah, don’t be shy. They’re very brave.

00:08:32.459 --> 00:08:33.125
Big time.

00:08:33.125 --> 00:08:35.334
And the most important female that’s joined us

00:08:35.334 --> 00:08:37.876
this year is magnificent Sarah Niles.

00:08:37.876 --> 00:08:38.709
Sarah Niles!

00:08:38.709 --> 00:08:39.959
And I would like to genuinely put

00:08:39.959 --> 00:08:42.584
in a bit of a complaint, in fact I did to Jason.

00:08:42.584 --> 00:08:44.125
I was like I would’ve liked to

00:08:44.125 --> 00:08:45.626
have more to do with Sarah.

00:08:45.626 --> 00:08:46.417
With her. 

00:08:46.417 --> 00:08:48.584
Because yes, the stuff we did in here

00:08:48.584 --> 00:08:51.542
with Sarah I was like oh oh oh oh oh oh oh!

00:08:51.542 --> 00:08:54.042
The first read through that we had on Zoom

00:08:54.042 --> 00:08:56.918
and she started reading that character

00:08:56.918 --> 00:08:59.334
of a therapist, sports therapist and I was like...

00:08:59.334 --> 00:09:02.667
She brought a very chilled out,  

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:06.792
effortless power and is a brilliant foil

00:09:06.792 --> 00:09:09.626
to where yours and my characters are.

00:09:09.626 --> 00:09:11.250
But also has an arc that, 

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:13.584
audiences be excited because again,

00:09:13.584 --> 00:09:15.083
as per usual with Ted Lasso,

00:09:15.083 --> 00:09:16.459
don’t judge a book by its cover.

00:09:16.459 --> 00:09:17.584
Yeah.

00:09:17.584 --> 00:09:18.959
Maybe this time next year we’ll be able

00:09:18.959 --> 00:09:19.834
to have her on the couch too.

00:09:19.834 --> 00:09:20.584
Yes.

00:09:21.792 --> 00:09:23.918
I will never forget that moment where somebody

00:09:23.918 --> 00:09:26.709
said to us “this is a show I want to show my daughter"

00:09:26.709 --> 00:09:28.459
"because of the relationship you two have created.”  

00:09:28.459 --> 00:09:30.751
And it really took the wind out of us both, didn’t it?

00:09:30.751 --> 00:09:32.834
That’s the highest compliment we could get.

